// Regression: barlines are score-synchronized — the repeat and its two endings appear on
// BOTH staves (Timing is score-level), the system start must join the staves with a bar,
// and inside a grand staff every barline spans the inter-staff gap (Span_bar).
//
// ⚠️ THIS BOOK USED TO CLAIM SOMETHING IT CAN NO LONGER SAY, and that is written down
// rather than quietly swapped for a different test (RULES §5.4). Until 2026-08-31 the
// repeat was written IN THE rh PART ALONE — `phrase rhTune { |: g'4 a g f | [1. …] :| … }`
// — and the claim was that a one-part repeat still draws on both staves. LYS1034 moved
// repeat structure to the form, so "written in one part" is not a spelling any more: a
// form's repeat is score-level by construction. What survives, and is what this snapshot
// still guards, is the DRAWING: both staves take the repeat barlines and the volta
// brackets, the system opens with a joining bar, and every bar spans the gap.
//
// ⚠️ AND THE RE-CUT MOVED BOTH OUTPUTS, on purpose and measured.
//   SOUND: 18 MIDI notes became 20. The music-side `|:` expanded ONLY the part it was
//   written in, so lh played its three bars once while rh played four; a form's repeat
//   expands the score, so lh repeats too. The page always treated the repeat as
//   score-level, so the picture and the sound used to disagree about this very book —
//   and the spelling that could disagree no longer exists.
//   PAGE: eight elements ADDED, none removed (masked diff, data-pos aside) — the two
//   volta brackets and their bold "1." / "2.", which the inline spelling drew NOWHERE in
//   this book. Everything else is byte-identical, including every barline.
time 4/4

part rh {
  clef treble
}

part lh {
  clef bass
}

// ⚠️ The phrases are kept, one bar each, because this book is also one of the 58 that
// LilyPondExporterTests.TheNotDeclaredWarning_NeverNamesAPhraseTheBookDeclares counts —
// re-cutting the music inline dropped that floor to 57.
phrase rhHead { g'4 a g f | }
phrase rhEnd1 { e2 d | }
phrase rhEnd2 { e2 c | }
phrase lhBass { c2 g | }

section Main {
  rh { rhHead }
  lh { lhBass }
}

section End1 {
  rh { rhEnd1 }
  lh { lhBass }
}

section End2 {
  rh { rhEnd2 }
  lh { lhBass }
}

form main { |: Main [1. ~End1] :| [2. ~End2] }

score main "grandstaff-repeat" {
  grandStaff {
    staff rh
    staff lh
  }
}
